{"text": "downstairs", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">down-</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">stair</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-s</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Located on a lower floor.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Adverb", "definitions": [{"definition": "Down the stairs.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(figurative) In or to hell.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(slang, euphemistic) Regarding the genitalia.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "In particular, especially historically, the servants\u2019 quarters.\n\n", "quote": [{"citation": "1978, Tom Reamy, Blind Voices:", "text": "Now the two of them rattled around in the old house, even with his office and small clinic sharing the downstairs with the kitchen, parlor, and dining room."}], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "The lower floor of a house, at ground level, or sometimes below.\n\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(slang, euphemistic) The genitalia.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["General American", "/da\u028an\u02c8st\u025b\u0279z/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/da\u028an\u02c8st\u025b\u0259z/"]]}